From: Tim Michals <tcmichals@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: sunxi-pck600: properly manage power domain states

At boot, sunxi_pck600_probe initializes power domains with
pm_genpd_init(&pd->genpd, NULL, false), passing is_off = false.
This incorrectly tells genpd that all domains are already powered on
in hardware. When consumer drivers probe and attach via genpd_dev_pm_attach(),
genpd checks genpd_status_on(genpd), assumes the domain is already on,
and skips calling .power_on().

Initialize peripheral domains with is_off = true so genpd explicitly
invokes .power_on() when consumer drivers attach, properly configuring
hardware PPU power switches and deasserting power gates. Also add
informational log messages in sunxi_pck600_probe() and
sunxi_pck600_pd_set_power() to trace domain transitions.

Signed-off-by: Tim Michals <tcmichals@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
@@ -91,6 +91,9 @@ static int sunxi_pck600_pd_set_power(struct sunxi_pck600_pd *pd, bool on)
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(pck->dev, "failed to turn domain \"%s\" %s: %d\n",
 			genpd->name, str_on_off(on), ret);
+	else
+		dev_info(pck->dev, "turned domain \"%s\" %s (PWSR=0x%08x)\n",
+			 genpd->name, str_on_off(on), readl(pd->base + PPU_PWSR));
 
 	return ret;
 }
@@ -183,7 +186,10 @@ static int sunxi_pck600_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		pd->base = base + PPU_REG_SIZE * i;
 
 		sunxi_pck600_pd_setup(pd, desc);
-		ret = pm_genpd_init(&pd->genpd, NULL, false);
+		dev_info(dev, "PD[%d] %s: base=%px PWSR=0x%08x PWPR=0x%08x\n",
+			 i, desc->pd_names[i], pd->base,
+			 readl(pd->base + PPU_PWSR), readl(pd->base + PPU_PWPR));
+		ret = pm_genpd_init(&pd->genpd, NULL, true);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to initialize power domain\n");
 			goto err_remove_pds;
